From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "D.R.racer" <drracer@seznam.cz>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 23:28:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wayland: convert tiled strides of DMA_DRM buffers to
 bytes

With DMA_DRM caps, gst_wl_linux_dmabuf_construct_wl_buffer() takes the
format info from the caps (GST_VIDEO_FORMAT_DMA_DRM), so get_drm_stride()
does not see that the video meta's strides are GstVideo tile strides and
sends them unconverted: a 1920x1080 NV12_32L32 buffer (Allwinner video
engine, NV12 + DRM_FORMAT_MOD_ALLWINNER_TILED) gets stride 0x22003c, which
the compositor rejects ("invalid buffer stride or height for plane 0").

Use the video meta's format when it is a real format.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 wayland/gstwllinuxdmabuf.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/gst-libs/gst/wayland/gstwllinuxdmabuf.c b/gst-libs/gst/wayland/gstwllinuxdmabuf.c
index 54c5811..b3f540e 100644
--- a/gst-libs/gst/wayland/gstwllinuxdmabuf.c
+++ b/gst-libs/gst/wayland/gstwllinuxdmabuf.c
@@ -125,7 +125,15 @@ gst_wl_linux_dmabuf_construct_wl_buffer (GstBuffer * buf,
 
   vmeta = gst_buffer_get_video_meta (buf);
   if (vmeta) {
-    finfo = drm_info->vinfo.finfo;
+    /* The meta strides follow the meta's format: for a tiled format they
+     * are GstVideo tile strides, which get_drm_stride() must convert. The
+     * DMA_DRM caps format does not say whether the layout is tiled. */
+    if (vmeta->format != GST_VIDEO_FORMAT_DMA_DRM &&
+        vmeta->format != GST_VIDEO_FORMAT_UNKNOWN &&
+        vmeta->format != GST_VIDEO_FORMAT_ENCODED)
+      finfo = gst_video_format_get_info (vmeta->format);
+    else
+      finfo = drm_info->vinfo.finfo;
     width = vmeta->width;
     height = vmeta->height;
     nplanes = vmeta->n_planes;
